  "slug": "tally-customer-supplier-ledger-lookup",
  "title": "Finding the Correct Customer or Supplier Ledger in Tally Data",
  "description": "Use party names, opening context and a known transaction when two ledger names look alike.",
  "category": "Ledgers and PDFs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Start with exact names",
      "body": "Open the company and use the party name as it appears in TallyPrime. For instance, Sunrise Traders and Sunrise Trading are two example names that can look similar in a search. Avoid selecting the first result just because the beginning matches."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check a known transaction",
      "body": "Open the possible ledger and compare a recent transaction you can identify with a source voucher. Match the period, number and amount. If the voucher is absent in both candidates, check your date range and successful sync before drawing a conclusion."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Use the name as recorded in the books",
      "body": "When sending a PDF or asking support for help, use the exact ledger name and company. If the names are intentionally similar, add a known voucher number to the request so your colleague opens the same ledger."
    }
  ],
  "relatedPaths": [
    "/guides/tally-ledger-on-mobile",
    "/for-accountants"
  ]
}
